  "name": "FSH AND LH STIMULATION BY GONADOTROPIN RELEASING HORMONE(GNRH)",
  "code": "1761",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"95\" data-end=\"377\"><strong data-start=\"95\" data-end=\"120\">GnRH stimulation test</strong> assesses the <strong data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"238\">pituitary gland's ability to release FSH (Follicle-Stimulating Hormone) and LH (Luteinizing Hormone)</strong> in response to synthetic GnRH. It helps evaluate disorders of <strong data-start=\"301\" data-end=\"312\">puberty</strong>, <strong data-start=\"314\" data-end=\"339\">reproductive function</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"345\" data-end=\"376\">pituitary&ndash;hypothalamic axis</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"679\" data-end=\"707\"><strong data-start=\"683\" data-end=\"707\">Clinical Indications</strong></p>\n<ol data-start=\"708\" data-end=\"914\">\n<li data-start=\"708\" data-end=\"730\">\n<p data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"730\"><strong data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"730\">Delayed puberty</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"731\" data-end=\"756\">\n<p data-start=\"734\" data-end=\"756\"><strong data-start=\"734\" data-end=\"756\">Precocious puberty</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"757\" data-end=\"817\">\n<p data-start=\"760\" data-end=\"817\"><strong data-start=\"760\" data-end=\"817\">Differentiating hypothalamic vs pituitary dysfunction</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"818\" data-end=\"854\">\n<p data-start=\"821\" data-end=\"854\"><strong data-start=\"821\" data-end=\"854\">Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"914\">\n<p data-start=\"858\" data-end=\"914\"><strong data-start=\"858\" data-end=\"914\">Congenital GnRH deficiency (e.g., Kallmann syndrome)</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>FSH/LH Response to GnRH</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Central precocious puberty (CPP)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Exaggerated rise</strong>, especially in <strong>LH</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Peripheral precocious puberty</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No significant rise</strong> (pituitary not involved)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Constitutional delay of puberty</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blunted response</strong>, but may improve with age</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Absent or minimal response</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hypergonadotropic hypogonadism</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Elevated baseline LH/FSH</strong>, exaggerated or normal response</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
